cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this report, please cite it using the metadata from this file."
title: "Hypothesis failure for Ioana's Theorem 8.2 under a twisted comultiplication"
type: report
authors:
  - family-names: Fredriksen
    given-names: Daniel Eric
    affiliation: "Quantyra Inc"
url: "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.21859653"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Quantyra/connes-rigidity"
license: CC-BY-4.0
version: "0.1.2-report"
keywords:
  - Connes rigidity
  - Ioana
  - operator algebras
  - Quantyra
  - Nielsen
abstract: >-
  Bounded public report: Ioana's Theorem 8.2 (JAMS 2011) does not apply to the
  twisted comultiplication Θ(f u_g)=f u_g ⊗ Φ(u_g) because hypothesis (2) fails
  by the by-construction containment im(Θ) ⊆ A_G ⊗̄ L(H). Does not prove or
  refute Connes rigidity and does not settle OpenAI or Zhou counterexamples.
  Companion Lean tag v0.1.1-obstruction (DOI 10.5281/zenodo.21859309).
  Version DOI 10.5281/zenodo.21859653; concept DOI 10.5281/zenodo.21845586.
